Source: pulseaudio
Section: libs
Priority: optional
Maintainer: crick Debian Backports <backports@users.noreply.github.com>
# Упаковка взята из Debian (pulseaudio_17.0+dfsg1-2) и переработана: публикуется
# только клиентская часть.
#   * демон не собирается (-Ddaemon=false): не публикуются пакеты pulseaudio,
#     pulseaudio-utils, pulseaudio-equalizer, pulseaudio-module-* и libpulsedsp.
#     Pulseaudio нужен этому репозиторию только как зависимость клиентских
#     библиотек - их используют mpv (ao_pulse) и sfwbar (pulsectl.c);
#   * X11 выключен (-Dx11=disabled): штатный libpulse0 из trixie зависит от
#     libx11-6, libx11-xcb1 и libxcb1, что нарушает правило репозитория "X11
#     нет нигде". Ни один символ из libpulse0.symbols при этом не исчезает:
#     единственный X11-код в библиотеке - pa_client_conf_from_x11(), который
#     нужен только для автозапуска pax11publish;
#   * JACK выключен (-Djack=disabled) по правилу репозитория;
#   * возможности демона выключены: ALSA, Bluetooth, GStreamer, LIRC, RAOP
#     (openssl), resample (soxr/speex), FFTW, orc, avahi, udev, tcpwrap,
#     WebRTC/adrian AEC, GSettings. Из-за -Ddaemon=false они всё равно не
#     собираются, но выключены явно;
#   * libpulsedsp не собирается (-Doss-output=disabled): это OSS-обёртка для
#     устаревших программ, а не то, что нужно mpv и sfwbar;
#   * man-страницы, doxygen и тесты не собираются (-Dman=false
#     -Ddoxygen=false -Dtests=false);
#   * dbgsym-пакеты не собираются (общее правило scripts/build-package.sh).
# Правила отключения — в правилах проекта.
Build-Depends:
 debhelper-compat (= 13),
 gettext,
 m4,
 meson,
 ninja-build,
 pkgconf,
 libasyncns-dev,
 libdbus-1-dev,
 libglib2.0-dev,
 libsndfile1-dev,
 libsystemd-dev
Standards-Version: 4.7.0
Homepage: https://www.freedesktop.org/software/pulseaudio/
Vcs-Git: https://salsa.debian.org/debian/pulseaudio.git
Vcs-Browser: https://salsa.debian.org/debian/pulseaudio

Package: libpulse0
Section: libs
Architecture: any
Multi-Arch: same
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Description: PulseAudio client libraries
 PulseAudio, previously known as Polypaudio, is a sound server for POSIX and
 WIN32 systems. It is a drop in replacement for the ESD sound server with
 much better latency, mixing/re-sampling quality and overall architecture.
 .
 Client libraries used by applications that access a PulseAudio sound server
 via PulseAudio's native interface.
 .
 This build has no X11 support at all, so unlike the libpulse0 of Debian it
 pulls in none of the X11 client libraries. The daemon itself is not published
 here; use pipewire from this repository instead.

Package: libpulse-mainloop-glib0
Section: libs
Architecture: any
Multi-Arch: same
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Description: PulseAudio client libraries (glib support)
 PulseAudio, previously known as Polypaudio, is a sound server for POSIX and
 WIN32 systems. It is a drop in replacement for the ESD sound server with
 much better latency, mixing/re-sampling quality and overall architecture.
 .
 Client libraries used by applications that access a PulseAudio sound server
 via PulseAudio's native interface.
 .
 This package adds support for glib2 client applications.

Package: libpulse-dev
Section: libdevel
Architecture: any
Multi-Arch: same
Depends: ${misc:Depends},
 libpulse0 (= ${binary:Version}),
 libpulse-mainloop-glib0 (= ${binary:Version}),
 libglib2.0-dev
Description: PulseAudio client development headers and libraries
 PulseAudio, previously known as Polypaudio, is a sound server for POSIX and
 WIN32 systems. It is a drop in replacement for the ESD sound server with
 much better latency, mixing/re-sampling quality and overall architecture.
 .
 Headers and libraries for developing applications that access a PulseAudio
 sound server via PulseAudio's native interface.